{
  "date": "2026-10-18",
  "period_start": "2026-10-11",
  "period_end": "2026-10-17",
  "title": "Sandboxes became places to keep working",
  "summary": "This week made Pollinations a more complete place to build: longer-lived sandboxes, more kinds of generation, and fewer obstacles between an idea and an API call.\n\nSandbox timeouts can extend beyond a day, with daily restarts preserving files, memory and processes but dropping open connections. A new Enter page brings creation, SSH instructions and lifecycle controls together. Names, faster repeat SSH connections, more template tools and Machines MCP give people and agents more ways to use those environments. Support for an opt-in larger template was added; the change did not create the underlying E2B template.\n\nThe catalog gained short-video generation with Kandinsky, image generation and editing with Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo, new chat models, two Lightning Text versions, and models for typed decisions. Mirelo adds synchronized sound effects to a source video. OpenAI speech gained adjustable speed, while image references, video dimensions, provider routing and transcription formats received fixes.\n\nImage, video, audio and 3D requests can use `Prefer: respond-async`, then retrieve job status and results through the API or SDK. The SDK also added 3D generation, speech with word timings, model-status queries, React generation hooks and an AI SDK chat transport. Follow-up fixes covered retries, cached results and request windows—the details that matter once jobs stop fitting neatly inside one HTTP connection.\n\nMarkdown docs, discovery headers, Agent Skills and callable agent model IDs make the API easier for agents to find and use. Computer MCP gained JavaScript execution, Machines MCP gained sandbox controls, and community PR-review agents joined the catalog. Polli also queues Discord follow-ups instead of rejecting messages that arrive while it works.",
  "pr_count": 257,
